# ADD LIVE IN-BROWSER PYTHON CODE EDITOR & RUNNER (`24b3007`) Add a feature where learners can write, edit, and run Python code directly inside the website with instant console output. Implement this cleanly in `src/` and verify with `npm run build`: --- ## 1. BUILD `<PythonRunner />` COMPONENT (`src/components/PythonRunner.tsx`) 1. **Real Python Execution in the Browser (Pyodide via CDN):** * Load Pyodide (`https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/pyodide/v0.26.4/full/pyodide.js`) cleanly on the client (cached on `window` so it loads only once) and show a small status badge (`"Loading Python..."` -> `"Python 3 Ready"`). * When the learner clicks **"
\f14 \uc0\u9654 
\f0  Run Code"** (or presses `Ctrl+Enter` / `Cmd+Enter`), capture `sys.stdout` and `sys.stderr`, execute the code, and display the exact printed output inside a clean terminal output box below the editor (preserving leading spaces so star patterns like `*`, `**`, `***` render accurately). * Add a quick safety check before running (e.g., reject raw `while True:` without `break`) so an infinite loop never freezes the browser tab. 2. **Ergonomic Python Code Editor (No Lost Focus on `Tab`):** * Render a crisp monospace code editor (`JetBrains Mono` / `Fira Code`) with line numbers, a **"
\f14 \uc0\u9654 
\f0  Run Code"** button, and a **"
\f8 \uc0\u8634 
\f0  Reset Code"** button. * **Handle `Tab` and `Enter` keys properly:** Pressing `Tab` inserts 4 spaces (`" "`) instead of jumping focus away from the editor, and pressing `Enter` after a line ending with `:` automatically indents the next line by 4 spaces. 3. **Calm, `L5`-Friendly Error Translation:**[cite: 7, 11] * If the learner's Python code raises an `IndentationError`, `SyntaxError`, or `NameError`, display the message calmly (never scary flashing red) with a 1-line plain-English hint (e.g., *"Tip: Lines inside a `for` loop need 4 spaces of indentation"*)[cite: 7, 11]. --- ## 2. INTEGRATE LIVE CODE RUNNING ACROSS THE APP 1. **Inside Coding & Bug-Fix Exercises:** * Embed `<PythonRunner />` directly into all code-writing / bug-fix exercises so learners can modify the loop, click **"
\f14 \uc0\u9654 
\f0  Run Code"** to test their output live as many times as they want, and then submit their code + live console output + written explanation to `/api/tutor`. 2. **Interactive `"Try It Live"` Playground:** * Add a collapsible **"
\f9 \uc0\u55357 \u56507 
\f0  Live Python Scratchpad"** drawer/button in the workspace header (and a **"Try This Example Live"** button on the lesson walkthrough snippets) so learners can write and run any custom loop or `*` pattern code at any point during their 10-minute session[cite: 7]. --- ## 3. PRESERVE IDENTITY & VERIFY * Keep **`Roll No: 24b3007`** visible in the footer of every screen and on `/about`[cite: 2, 8]. * Update `README.md` to document the live in-browser Python execution engine, and run `npm run build` to ensure zero build or TypeScript errors.\
